# The Contractor may sacrifice itself (it is "a creature", already on the battlefield as its trigger resolves), and the reflexive
# trigger still happens (CR 603.12): with no other creature Bot1 chooses itself as "target player" and draws two cards (three left
# in hand after the Moxen and the Contractor, so five) and loses 2 life (20 to 18), while Bot2 is untouched (pair of the opponent scenario).

[Bot1 Deck]
Unscrupulous Contractor
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Unscrupulous Contractor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Unscrupulous Contractor)
Bot1.Target(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Unscrupulous Contractor
Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot2.Hand.Count = 7
Bot2.Life = 20
